# The PowerShell script is stored with LF in the repository and checked out
# with CRLF, and it carries a UTF-8 BOM on purpose: Windows PowerShell 5.1 uses
# the BOM to read the non-ASCII keyword literals in the symptom router
# correctly. The BOM is file content, so it survives either way; CI checks it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
